<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 2-yr T-bills yield 20.99 pct at auction.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 2-yr T-bills yield 20.99 pct at auction.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of two-year MKM discount Treasury bills was 20.99 percent at the first auction of the paper on June 30, the National Bank said. Details of the first auction:</p>
<p>					   June 30</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ52K0107998</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  200</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,713</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 200</p>
<p> Annual yield			  20.99</p>
<p> Tenor				   2 years</p>
<p> Maturity				July 1, 1999</p>
<p>In contrast to the current three-, six- and 12-month T-bills, two-year paper is coupon-bearing, paying yields twice a year.</p>
<p>Coupons on the first issue are due to be paid on January 1, 1998, on July 2, 1998, on January 7, 1998 and July 1, 1999.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
